WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:15.979
was so happy!

2
00:00:15.999 --> 00:00:21.803
He was married to his beautiful princess and lived in his grand palace.

3
00:00:23.163 --> 00:00:25.865
Aladdin had forgotten about the evil magician.

4
00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:31.328
But Magrib had not forgotten about the lamp, my young friends.

5
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.480
Oh no.

6
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.441
Magrib never stopped thinking about it.

7
00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:43.643
In fact, he had used a spell to create a blue crystal ball that could find anything.

8
00:00:44.924 --> 00:00:47.905
He hoped to see the magic lamp through the mist in the ball.

9
00:00:49.505 --> 00:00:52.726
"Oh, I can see inside the enchanted treasury!"

10
00:00:53.206 --> 00:00:55.027
he said, staring into the ball.

11
00:00:55.047 --> 00:00:59.128
"Hmmm—but where is the lamp?"

12
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:04.375
He moved around the crystal ball, hoping to get a better view.

13
00:01:04.395 --> 00:01:07.177
"I don't see the lamp.

14
00:01:07.898 --> 00:01:09.459
I don't see that boy either.

15
00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:11.721
He should be lying there dead."

16
00:01:13.002 --> 00:01:15.404
Magrib paced up and down his room.

17
00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:21.269
Then he pressed his bony hands against the sides of the crystal ball.

18
00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:24.731
"Show me where Aladdin is!"

19
00:01:25.332 --> 00:01:26.573
demanded the magician.

20
00:01:27.994 --> 00:01:29.936
He looked deep into the mist again.

21
00:01:31.364 --> 00:01:31.924
"What's this?"

22
00:01:32.745 --> 00:01:33.405
he hissed.

23
00:01:34.866 --> 00:01:36.166
His face grew dark.

24
00:01:36.786 --> 00:01:38.687
His pale eyes flashed.

25
00:01:40.668 --> 00:01:45.550
Magrib saw Aladdin in a palace, not dead in the enchanted treasury.

26
00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:51.232
He was dressed in fine clothes and walking with a beautiful woman.

27
00:01:52.493 --> 00:01:54.834
"He is alive," cried Magrib.

28
00:01:56.195 --> 00:01:57.035
"He is rich!"

29
00:01:57.875 --> 00:01:59.236
He looked into the ball again.

30
00:02:00.532 --> 00:02:02.393
"And he has married a princess!"

31
00:02:04.413 --> 00:02:09.775
That day, before the sun set, the magician was on his way back to Aladdin's home.

32
00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:12.515
"I'll find him again!"

33
00:02:13.075 --> 00:02:13.556
he said.

34
00:02:13.576 --> 00:02:17.016
"And this time, I'll get the lamp!"

35
00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:24.178
When Magrib arrived in Aladdin's city, everyone he passed was talking about Aladdin's palace.

36
00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:29.780
"It's grander than the sultan's," one man said.

37
00:02:31.036 --> 00:02:32.217
"Wait until you see it!"

38
00:02:32.237 --> 00:02:35.400
"It is the magic of the lamp!"

39
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.761
Magrib growled to himself.

40
00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:39.863
He turned to the man.

41
00:02:39.883 --> 00:02:41.885
"Where is his palace?"

42
00:02:43.966 --> 00:02:49.010
The man pointed the way, and then added, "But Aladdin's not home.

43
00:02:49.651 --> 00:02:51.212
He's away hunting for a week."

44
00:02:52.633 --> 00:02:56.036
When the wicked Magrib heard this, he thought of a plan.

45
00:02:57.376 --> 00:03:00.859
The next day, he went and bought a dozen new lamps.

46
00:03:02.941 --> 00:03:05.403
They looked exactly like the magic lamp.

47
00:03:06.664 --> 00:03:10.407
Magrib dressed in rags and carried the lamps through the streets.

48
00:03:10.427 --> 00:03:14.470
"Who will trade an old lamp for a new lamp?"

49
00:03:15.091 --> 00:03:15.851
he called out.

50
00:03:16.632 --> 00:03:18.733
People shook their heads when they heard him.

51
00:03:18.754 --> 00:03:21.436
"New for old?"

52
00:03:22.196 --> 00:03:23.057
a woman laughed.

53
00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:26.460
"Whoever heard of such a silly trade?"

54
00:03:28.468 --> 00:03:30.469
Magrib did not pay any attention.

55
00:03:31.789 --> 00:03:38.592
He went up and down the streets, shouting louder and louder, "Who will trade an old lamp for

56
00:03:38.652 --> 00:03:39.252
a new one?"

57
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:43.674
Slowly, he made his way to Aladdin's palace.

58
00:03:45.835 --> 00:03:49.677
Princess Badra and her attendants sat by an open window in the palace.

59
00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:55.239
They were eating fruit sherbets and sewing pretty scarves with silk thread.

60
00:03:55.259 --> 00:03:57.600
"What is that noise?"

61
00:03:58.276 --> 00:03:59.537
asked Princess Badra.

62
00:03:59.557 --> 00:04:01.338
"Who is shouting?"

63
00:04:03.559 --> 00:04:05.560
One of her attendants ran to the window.

64
00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:09.583
"Who will trade an old lamp for a new lamp?"

65
00:04:10.143 --> 00:04:11.004
called Magrib.

66
00:04:12.304 --> 00:04:14.526
The attendant at the window started laughing.

67
00:04:14.546 --> 00:04:18.548
"What are you laughing about, girl?"

68
00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:20.129
asked the princess.

69
00:04:20.149 --> 00:04:23.311
"A madman!"

70
00:04:23.831 --> 00:04:24.812
cried the attendant.

71
00:04:26.144 --> 00:04:28.765
"He wants to trade his new lamps for old ones!"

72
00:04:30.105 --> 00:04:32.806
When Princess Badra heard this, she jumped up.

73
00:04:34.066 --> 00:04:36.747
"We have an old brass lamp," she said.

74
00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.247
"I'll go and get it."

75
00:04:39.388 --> 00:04:41.368
Princess Badra ran out of the room.

76
00:04:43.529 --> 00:04:47.290
When she returned, she was carrying Aladdin's wonderful lamp.

77
00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.611
"Here," she said to a servant.

78
00:04:50.631 --> 00:04:54.152
"Take this dirty, old lamp downstairs.

79
00:04:55.421 --> 00:04:57.487
Let's see if that man is telling the truth.

80
00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.957
Here is an old lamp for a new one!"
